// DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE from a documented upstream bug.
//
// Upstream's Maude reply parser classifies an identifier as a user-defined AC
// symbol by SUBSTRING containment of the four encoding markers over the whole
// encoded identifier, the user's own function name included
// (`appIdent`, lib/term/src/Term/Maude/Parser.hs).  `tamXCAbar/1` encodes to
// `tamXCFUtamXCAbar`, which contains `tamXCA`, so every Maude reply carrying
// this application is rebuilt as an AC term — and `fAppAC _ [a] = a` then
// deletes the unary application outright.
//
// The port classifies by DECODING the attribute block instead
// (`tamarin_term::maude_parse::is_ac_fct_ident`), so it keeps the application.
// The `builtins: multiset` and the reducible `fst(<_, _>)` are what force the
// term through Maude; renaming the function is the only change needed to make
// both engines agree.
//
// Compared slice: the whole `theory … end` echo (see check.sh), which carries
// the closed rule both engines disagree about.

theory MarkerNorm
begin

builtins: multiset
functions: tamXCAbar/1

rule Gen:
  [ In(a), In(y) ] --[ D() ]-> [ Out(fst(<tamXCAbar(a), y>) ++ y) ]

lemma triv: exists-trace "Ex #i. D() @ i"

end
